@namespace TheCanalaveLibrary.SharedUI
@using TheCanalaveLibrary.Core

@* "Also posted on" links row (Feature 53). Placement is settled: near the bottom of the story
   page — after the chapter list, before recommendations — in subdued metadata styling. It exists
   for awareness (and the anti-theft reporting signal), not to invite clicking away.

   Display model (WU39, settled 2026-07-24, audit/Moderation.md F53) — deliberately NO checkmark:
   a checkmark asserts one-time-judgment-as-permanent-trust and invites the exact complacency the
   feature exists to avoid. A reviewed link instead shows a muted "reviewed · author's account:
   <handle>" sub-line linking to the confirmed external profile — inviting the reader to click
   through and compare, every time, rather than reassuring them nothing needs checking.
   Never-requested / pending / rejected links are deliberately IDENTICAL to the reader (a plain
   link) — reporting is driven by a reader's own outside knowledge that a story belongs to someone
   else, never by this internal state; an "unverified" flag would catch ~nobody and only cast
   suspicion on slow-but-legitimate authors. No dates anywhere in this UI (considered and rejected
   as overengineering — see audit/Moderation.md F53).

   Both link levels open in a new tab (rel=nofollow — author/mod-supplied external URLs).
   Pure leaf — no service injection. Renders nothing when there are no links. *@

@if (Links.Count > 0)
{
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-1.5 text-xs text-(--color-text-muted)">
        <span class="font-medium">Also posted on</span>
        @foreach (StoryExternalLinkDto link in Links)
        {
            <div class="flex flex-col">
                <a href="@link.Url" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow"
                   class="w-fit text-(--color-action-ink) hover:underline">
                    @link.PlatformName<span aria-hidden="true"> ↗</span><span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span>
                </a>
                @if (link.IsReviewed && link.AuthorAccountHandle is not null && link.AuthorAccountProfileUrl is not null)
                {
                    <span class="pl-3">
                        reviewed · author's account:
                        <a href="@link.AuthorAccountProfileUrl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow"
                           class="hover:underline" title="A moderator confirmed this link's authorship">
                            @link.AuthorAccountHandle<span aria-hidden="true"> ↗</span><span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span>
                        </a>
                    </span>
                }
            </div>
        }
    </div>
}

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public IReadOnlyList<StoryExternalLinkDto> Links { get; set; } = [];
}
